architecture domain-control
  canonical_name DomainControl
  family external
  domain External reality / DNS authority
  layer boundary
  semantic_question How can Bonfyre observe and deliberately publish the owned domain records without treating registrar state, a local plan, or a secret as canonical institutional truth?
  purpose Native Namecheap Dynamic DNS control for the owned Aurekai domains. It observes the public A record, distinguishes known parking ranges, plans a target, and requires an explicit apply boundary plus a per-domain credential before emitting an external effect.
  maturity implemented
  owns DomainPublicationIntent
  owns DNSObservation
  owns DNSPublicationReceipt
  consumes ExternalAuthority
  consumes AddressConstellation
  publishes DNSObservation
  publishes DomainPublicationReceipt
  node_types OwnedDomain
  node_types DNSObservation
  node_types DomainPublicationIntent
  node_types DNSPublicationReceipt
  edge_types observes_dns
  edge_types publishes_dns
  internal_calculus owned domain -> per-domain Dynamic DNS credential; current IPv4 -> parked|live observation
  internal_calculus status -> plan -> explicit apply; apply refuses absent credentials and never uses an implicit secrets path
  invariant a DNS plan is not an external publication effect
  invariant each publication requires one explicit IPv4 target and the specific owned-domain secret
  invariant public DNS observation is ForeignTwin state until reconciled with an effect receipt
  forbidden_inference possession of a domain credential -> authority over a Matrix subject, institution, or publication presence
  forbidden_inference an A record -> a working TLS edge, semantic route, or readable public object
  forbidden_inference a parked record -> loss of domain ownership
  native_format graf
  command bonfyre-domain
  source_path cmd/BonfyreDomain/src/main.c
  witness cmd/BonfyreDomain/tests/domain_control_test.sh
  source_lineage Namecheap owned-domain Dynamic DNS boundary recovered from scripts/akai_ddns.py.archive
  interacts domain-control-publishes-web-edge

interaction domain-control-publishes-web-edge
  source domain-control
  destination web-address-edge
  relation public_host_reachability_candidate
  preserves one explicitly selected owned hostname and its external publication receipt as an edge-reachability input
  drops registrar credential material, raw provider response body, and any implication that DNS alone realizes TLS, routing, or semantic publication
  forbidden_inference published DNS -> a Matrix address resolving or a public presence being authorized
  witness cmd/BonfyreDomain/tests/domain_control_test.sh
  binding cmd/BonfyreDomain/src/main.c
